// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : texts/Working 	Sheet : Drea_the_Hook 
//
// Script      : Xlstocontactdef.bat 
// Version     : 35 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Contact Name : Drea the Hook 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Name :
"P200501809" "Drea the Hook"
// ProfessionString :
// DescriptionString :
"P4068575212" "Drea the Hook made his living as a crab fisherman, until his boat, and everyone else on it, went down in the icy waters off the coast of Alaska. Since that day, Drea can't seem to shake his fear of the sea. He doesn't have much compunction about the deals he brokers for villains in Port Oakes, though he knows that innocents often pay the price. Drea's just looking to put away a chunk of change that'll buy him a cozy retirement in a nice, landlocked community. His dedication to that dream makes him a reliable source of information."
// HelloString :
"P801789530" "I ain't got anything for you right now, but check back after you pull off a couple more of your own capers."
// IDontKnowYouString :
"P3307032112" "I don't know you from Adam, bub. Maybe you want Mikey the Ear."
// FirstVisitString :
"P2239829834" "My name's Drea. That's all you need to know. The less we know about each other, the better for both of us, dig? You do your own thing out there, and if I get a tip on something big going down--like a bank heist in Paragon City--I'll put a coded message in the Rogue Isle Protector. Just make sure to check out the newspaper from time to time. If you pull one of these Paragon City jobs, then I can introduce you to contacts who have more jobs for you. You should be on the lookout for Contacts as well. Some guys have jobs for you and the only prerequisite is that you have previously proved yourself by earning a badge or something.<br><br><color deepskyblue>Performing a set number of Newspaper missions will get you a Mayhem Mission, where you rob a bank in Paragon City. After that you will earn a contact in this zone if any are available in your level range. In addition, there are some contacts (NPCS with yellow rings around their feet) that simply require you have a particular badge before they will issue their missions to you. Click on any NPC you see with a yellow ring to see if they have any jobs for you to do.</color>"
// NoTasksRemainingString :
"P2470131391" "I got nothing more that would interest you, {VillainName}."
// PlayerBusyString :
"P2287731411" "I see you're too busy for me right now. Lemme know when you've freed up some of your own schemes.  <br><br><color deepskyblue>Now that you've been introduced to your Broker, you can start scanning the Rogue Isles Protector, the local newspaper, for things going on in your current zone. You can then act on one of your 'Schemes' by selecting it from the newspaper, listed under your Contacts. <br><br>After every 3 successful Schemes, your Broker will  tip you off to Heists and other special missions, then introduce you to new Contacts with stories and missions of their own.</color>"
// ComeBackLaterString :
"P2368658531" "I know some things, but they're big. Too big for anyone below Threat Level {Level}."
// RelationshipChangeString_ToFriend :
"P563578005" "Well, well, {VillainName}. I think this may be the beginning of a beautiful friendship."
// RelationshipChangeString_ToConfidant :
"P2366229121" "You've made quite a rep out there, {VillainName}."
// LocationString :
"P3345659944" "Port Oakes"
// IntroString :
"P3720490652" "I'd like you to meet someone named Drea the Hook. He can get you intel on everybody in Port Oakes."
// IntroAcceptString :
"P1906228434" "Choose Drea the Hook"
// IntroSendoffString :
"P1042601697" "Drea's tied into a lot of seedy types. You figure out what you want to do, he can likely tell you where to go and who's in your way."
// IntroduceOneContact :
// IntroduceTwoContacts :
"P1173284174" "Couple <A HREF=CONTACTLINK_INTRODUCE>people</a> I know want to meet you."
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 


