// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : texts/Working 	Sheet : Mikey_the_Ear 
//
// Script      : Xlstocontactdef.bat 
// Version     : 35 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Contact Name : Mikey the Ear 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Name :
"P415171471" "Mikey the Ear"
// ProfessionString :
// DescriptionString :
"P3731797860" "Mikey has put his big ears to use. It's said he hears everything going on in Port Oakes. Some think he might even have mutant powers."
// HelloString :
"P239951722" "Hey, {VillainName}! I hear you've been on a crime spree. Nice work. Keep it up and I'll have something really big for you."
// IDontKnowYouString :
"P3502666094" "You sure you're looking for me? Maybe you want Drea the Hook instead."
// FirstVisitString :
"P2289388802" "It's an honor to meet you, {VillainName}. I'm Mikey the Ear. Snitch extraordinaire. When you've made a name for yourself, I'll let you in on some big jobs. I mean really big... like robbing banks in Paragon City big. I'll let you know when by putting a secret code in the Rogue Isle Protector. Look for it while you're planning your schemes and we'll make some serious moola together. Capiche?<br><br>Also, I ain't the only guy out there who has stuff for you to do... pulling off these jobs will get you introduced to some contacts who have some more specific stuff to do, and there's even guys just hangin' around the Rogue Isles who will just give you jobs if they think you are up to snuff. <br><br><color deepskyblue>Performing a set number of Newspaper missions will get you a Mayhem Mission, where you rob a bank in Paragon City. After that you will earn a contact in this zone if any are available in your level range. In addition, there are some contacts (NPCS with yellow rings around their feet) that simply require you have a particular badge before they will issue their missions to you. Click on any NPC you see with a yellow ring to see if they have any jobs for you to do.</color>"
// NoTasksRemainingString :
"P2442409929" "Sorry, friend. I ain't heard nothin' you'd be interested in."
// PlayerBusyString :
"P3926770233" "I hear you got enough goin' on right now, {VillainName}. Keep checkin' back though. I'll have something big for you eventually. <br><br><color deepskyblue>Now that you've been introduced to your Broker, you can start scanning the Rogue Isles Protector, the local newspaper, for things going on in your current zone. You can then act on one of your 'Schemes' by selecting it from the newspaper, listed under your Contacts. <br><br>After every 3 successful Schemes, your Broker will  tip you off to Heists and other special missions, then introduce you to new Contacts with stories and missions of their own.</color>"
// ComeBackLaterString :
"P1260527201" "I deal mostly with the big boys around here. Come back when you're Threat Level {Level} and I'll be happy to tell you everything I hear."
// RelationshipChangeString_ToFriend :
"P2124504879" "I hear bad things about you. And in the Rogue Isles, bad is good."
// RelationshipChangeString_ToConfidant :
"P1251757041" "You're doing some real damage out there, <VillainName>. I'm happy to be a part of your wrecking crew."
// LocationString :
// IntroString :
"P3260495686" "They say Mikey the Ear hears everything that takes place in Port Oakes."
// IntroAcceptString :
"P1565814320" "Choose Mikey the Ear"
// IntroSendoffString :
"P1633193927" "Mikey's got his ear to the ground in Port Oakes."
// IntroduceOneContact :
// IntroduceTwoContacts :
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 


